          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Colours"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Klik op + in de zijbalk. De naam is voor jou; adres, poort en gebruikersnaam zijn wat sssH gebruikt om te verbinden. Met groepen, labels en kleuren houd je een lange lijst leesbaar." : {
      "comment" : "Help: how to add a host",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "device" : {
              "ipad" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Tap + in the sidebar. The name is for you; the address, port, and username are what sssH uses to connect. Groups, labels, and colors keep a long list readable."
                }
              },
              "iphone" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Tap + in the sidebar. The name is for you; the address, port, and username are what sssH uses to connect. Groups, labels, and colors keep a long list readable."
                }
              },
              "mac" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Click + in the sidebar. The name is for you; the address, port, and username are what sssH uses to connect. Groups, labels, and colors keep a long list readable."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Tap + in the sidebar. The name is for you; the address, port, and username are what sssH uses to connect. Groups, labels, and colors keep a long list readable."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Klik op een host, of druk op ⌘K en typ de naam. Bij een eerste verbinding vraagt sssH je de hostsleutel te controleren; daarna waarschuwt het alleen als die verandert." : {
      "comment" : "Help: how to connect and what the host key prompt is",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "device" : {
              "ipad" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Tap a host, or press ⌘K and type its name. On a first connection, sssH asks you to check the host key; after that it only warns you if it changes."
                }
              },
              "iphone" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Tap a host, or press ⌘K and type its name. On a first connection, sssH asks you to check the host key; after that it only warns you if it changes."
                }
              },
              "mac" : {
