    "Meer" : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility label for the sidebar's overflow menu",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "More"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Meer regels kosten geheugen, per venster. Bij veel gesplitste vensters telt dat op." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the cost of a large scrollback",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "More lines cost memory, per pane. With many splits that adds up."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Meestal ~/.ssh/config. sssh leest het bestand alleen; er wordt niets aan veranderd." : {
      "comment" : "Explains where the config lives and that sssh does not modify it",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Usually ~/.ssh/config. sssh only reads the file; nothing is changed."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Meestal ~/.ssh/config. sssH leest het bestand alleen; er wordt niets aan veranderd." : {
      "comment" : "Explains where the config lives and that sssh does not modify it",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Usually ~/.ssh/config. sssH only reads the file; nothing is changed."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Meld aan als %@ op %@." : {
      "comment" : "Says which account on which host is being authenticated",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sign in as %@ on %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Melding sluiten" : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility label for dismissing a tunnel error",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dismiss message"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Met {{naam}} vraagt sssh om een waarde. {{naam=standaard}} vult er alvast een in. Accolades in shell-scripts blijven gewoon staan." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the snippet placeholder syntax",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "With {{name}}, sssh asks for a value. {{name=default}} fills one in. Braces in shell scripts are left alone."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Met {{naam}} vraagt sssH om een waarde. {{naam=standaard}} vult er alvast een in. Accolades in shell-scripts blijven gewoon staan." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the snippet placeholder syntax",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "With {{name}}, sssH asks for a value. {{name=default}} fills one in. Braces in shell scripts are left alone."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Met ⇧⌘I gaat wat je typt naar elk venster van het tabblad tegelijk — handig voor hetzelfde commando op meerdere servers. Het staat per tabblad aan of uit, en gaat niet stiekem mee naar het volgende." : {
      "comment" : "Help: input broadcast",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "With ⇧⌘I, what you type goes to every pane of the tab at once — handy for the same command on multiple servers. It is on or off per tab, and does not quietly carry over to the next one."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Met onderstaande regels stuurt je shell zelf de standaardmarkeringen (OSC 133). Andere terminals lezen ze ook, dus je zit nergens aan vast." : {
      "comment" : "Explains that the snippet uses a standard other terminals also read",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The lines below make your shell send the standard markers (OSC 133) itself. Other terminals read them too, so nothing here ties you to sssh."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Met shell-integratie verdeelt sssH de uitvoer in blokken: per opdracht zie je de opdracht zelf, de uitvoer en of die slaagde. De opdrachtenlijst open je met ⇧⌘B; de integratie stel je vanaf daar in." : {
      "comment" : "Help: what command blocks are",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "With shell integration, sssH divides the output into blocks: for each command you see the command itself, its output, and whether it succeeded. Open the command list with ⇧⌘B; you set up the integration from there."
          }
        }
      }
    },
